                                                height = 412
                                                dialogTitle = Explanation
                                                messageString = The OpenMotif Tree and Outline widget actually derive behavior from the\
Hierarchy Widget. The Hierarchy widget provides resources that specify\
the relationships between children.\
\
XmNautoClose specifies whether the Tree or Outline automatically closes\
any nodes if a parent node is closed. To see the behavior, press the Auto\
Close toggle, then close and reopen the Core.\
\
XmNnodeState is a constraint resource on a child of the Tree or Outline.\
It determines whether a node is Open, Closed, Hidden, or Always Visible.\
Use "Show Layout Code..." to see how this demo used this resource.\
\
XmNparentNode specifies this node's parent. This resource determines the\
node's logical parent (the widget instance tree says the node is a child of\
the Tree or Outline, but the parentNode will specify where on the layout\
the node will appear. Use "Show Layout Code..." to see how this demo used\
this resource.\
\
XmNnodeStateCallback provides a way to receive feedback when any node is\
opened or closed. To use this callback, press the Node State Callback toggle.
                                            }
                                        } explain
                                    }
                                } xmDialogShell0_2
